              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+topos"} well-pointed topos
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zorn%27s+lemma"} Zorn's lemma
          %p In principle, every article could explain how it applies to constructive mathematics, but that will probably never happen.
          %p There is also
          %ul
            %li
              %span.newWikiWord
                constructivism and idealism
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/constructivism+and+idealism"} ?
          %h2#References References
          %p
            See also the references at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+mathematics"} intuitionistic mathematics
            for more.
          %p Original texts:
          %ul
            %li#Bishop
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Errett+Bishop"}> Errett Bishop
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Foundations+of+Constructive+Analysis"} Foundations of Constructive Analysis
          %p rewritten as:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Errett+Bishop"}> Errett Bishop
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Bridges"} Douglas Bridges
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constructive+Analysis"} Constructive Analysis
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 279
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-61667-9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-61667-9
          %p Early monographs:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anne+Sjerp+Troelstra"}> Anne Sjerp Troelstra
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirk+van+Dalen"} Dirk van Dalen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constructivism in Mathematics – An introduction
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 121
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.elsevier.com/books/constructivism-in-mathematics-vol-1/troelstra/978-0-444-70266-1"} ISBN:9780444702661
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anne+Sjerp+Troelstra"}> Anne Sjerp Troelstra
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirk+van+Dalen"} Dirk van Dalen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constructivism in Mathematics – An introduction
                = succeed ":" do
                  %strong 123
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://shop.elsevier.com/books/constructivism-in-mathematics-vol-2/troelstra/978-0-444-70358-3"} ISBN:9780444703583
          %p Gentle introductions:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Bridges"}> Douglas Bridges
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introducing constructive mathematics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Bridges-IntroducingConstructiveMath.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Five Stages of Accepting Constructive Mathematics
                %strong 54
                (2017) 481-498 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/bull/1556"}> doi:10.1090/bull/1556
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/bull/2017-54-03/S0273-0979-2016-01556-4/S0273-0979-2016-01556-4.pdf"} pdf
              %p
                based on a talk at IAS (March 18, 2013) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://video.ias.edu/members/1213/0318-AndrejBauer"}> video
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Richman"}> Fred Richman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/modern-logic/volume-6/issue-3/Interview-with-a-constructive-mathematician/rml/1204835729.full"} Interview with a constructive mathematician
                %strong 6
                3 (1996) 247-271 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1400617"}> MathSciNet
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Blechschmidt15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Blechschmidt"}> Ingo Blechschmidt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Double-negation translation and CPS transforms
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://rawgit.com/iblech/talk-constructive-mathematics/master/negneg-translation-notes.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://plato.stanford.edu/entries/mathematics-constructive/"} Constructive mathematics
          %p
            An more technical introduction to constructive reasoning in mathematics is (with an eye towards
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
          %p Other accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+J.+Beeson"}> Michael J. Beeson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foundations of Constructive Mathematics
                %strong 3
                6, Springer 1985 (
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-642-68952-9"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-642-68952-9
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007%2F978-3-642-68952-9.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Bridges"} Douglas Bridges
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Richman"} Fred Richman
                %em Varieties of constructive mathematics
                (1987)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Richman"}> Fred Richman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Bridges"} Douglas Bridges
                = succeed "." do
                  %em A weak countable choice principle
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9939-00-05327-2"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9939-00-05327-2
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Makkai"} Michael Makkai
                (1996).
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.mcgill.ca/makkai/anafun/"} Avoiding the axiom of choice in general category theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Richman"}> Fred Richman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constructive Mathematics without Choice
              %p
                in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Reuniting the Antipodes – Constructive and Nonstandard Views of the Continuum
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 306
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-015-9757-9_17"} doi:10.1007/978-94-015-9757-9_17
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Taylor"} Paul Taylor
                (1996). Intuitionistic Sets and Ordinals. Available (with several other references) at
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.PaulTaylor.EU/ordinals/index.php"} Induction, recursion, replacement and the ordinals
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                (1995).
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Algebraic set theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Franka+Waaldijk"}> Franka Waaldijk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the foundations of constructive mathematics - especially in relation to the theory of continuous functions
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10699-004-3065-z"} doi:10.1007/s10699-004-3065-z
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.fwaaldijk.nl/foundations%20of%20constructive%20mathematics.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Auke+B.+Booij"}> Auke B. Booij
                , Analysis in univalent type theory (
                %a{:href => "https://etheses.bham.ac.uk/id/eprint/10411/7/Booij2020PhD.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            On constructive mathematics applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            (cf.
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computable+physics"} computable physics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+S.+Bridges"}> Douglas S. Bridges
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Can Constructive Mathematics Be Applied in Physics?
                %strong 28
                5 (1999) 439-453 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/30226680"}> jstor:30226680
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1004420413391"} doi:10.1023/A:1004420413391
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Intuitionistic Mathematics and Realizability in the Physical World
                %em A Computable Universe
                (2012) 143-157 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814374309_0008"}> doi:10.1142/9789814374309_0008
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://math.andrej.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/real-world-realizability.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://math.andrej.com/2014/03/04/intuitionistic-mathematics-and-realizability-in-the-physical-world/"} webpage
          %p
            In view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reverse+mathematics"} reverse mathematics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hajime+Ishihara"}> Hajime Ishihara
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Reverse Mathematics in Bishop’s Constructive Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4000/philosophiascientiae.406"} doi:10.4000/philosophiascientiae.406
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://philosophiascientiae.revues.org/pdf/406"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hannes+Diener"}> Hannes Diener
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constructive Reverse Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.05495"} arXiv:1804.05495
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dspace.ub.uni-siegen.de/handle/ubsi/1306"} dspace:ubsi/1306
          %p
            General comments on intuitionistic mathematics/logic as the natural language for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            are in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.andrej.com/2008/08/13/intuitionistic-mathematics-for-physics/"} Intuitionistic mathematics for physics
          %p
            For more on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            formalized in intuitionistic mathematics (notably in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
          %p
            For an emphasis on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+relevance"} proof relevance
          %ul
            %li#Harper13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Harper"}> Robert Harper
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://existentialtype.wordpress.com/2013/07/10/constructive-mathematics-is-not-meta-mathematics/"} Constructive Mathematics is not Metamathematics
              (2013)
          %p
            Most books on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            include some discussion of toposes'
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal
            constructive logic. One good reference is:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"} Peter Johnstone
              (2003).
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Sketches of an elephant
          %p A historical account is in
          %ul
            %li#Troelstra91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anne+Sjerp+Troelstra"}> Anne Sjerp Troelstra
              ,
              %em History of Constructivism in the Twentieth Century
              (1991) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.illc.uva.nl/Research/Publications/Reports/ML-1991-05.text.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Troelstra-HistoryOfConstructivism.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability"} realizability
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computability"} computability
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Bauer05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Realizability as connection between constructive and computable mathematics
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Weihrauch"} Klaus Weihrauch
              = succeed "," do
                %em CCA 2005 - Second International Conference on Computability and Complexity in Analysis
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.andrej.com/data/c2c.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            with constructive methods:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Lombardi"}> Henri Lombardi
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claude+Quitt%C3%A9"} Claude Quitté
              (2010):
              %em Commutative algebra: Constructive methods (Finite projective modules)
              Translated by Tania K. Roblo, Springer (2015) (
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-94-017-9944-7"}> doi:10.1007/978-94-017-9944-7
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://hlombardi.free.fr/CACM.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antithesis+interpretation"} antithesis interpretation
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %ul
            %li#Shulman2022
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Affine logic for constructive mathematics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/bsl.2022.28"} doi:10.1017/bsl.2022.28
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.07518"} arXiv:1805.07518
        .revisedby
